# WebinoERP — Core Rules

## Stack (mandatory)

- **Backend:** Laravel (latest stable). API-first only. Modular monolith via `nwidart/laravel-modules` under `backend/Modules/`.
- **Frontend:** Next.js App Router + official [shadcn/ui](https://ui.shadcn.com/).
- **Deploy:** Dockerized microservices — separate `frontend` and `backend` containers (`docker-compose.yml` / `docker-compose.aapanel.yml`). Never merge them into one runtime image for production.
- **Runtime:** Laravel Octane + FrankenPHP; reverse proxy Caddy (`web` is the only host-published service). Keep Reverb (`ws`) for realtime.

## Quality bar

- No placeholders, stubs, “TODO UI”, or fake data in shipped paths.
- Auth must be complete: no gaps in cookie/session/Sanctum, middleware gates, or setup redirects.
- No hard-coded user-facing strings (UI, errors, nav, empty states) — use i18n keys.
- Every visible site/admin setting (logo, colors, accent, copy, fonts) must be editable from the dashboard. Never ship a front-end value the operator cannot change.

## Architecture

- Modular: every feature and every third-party integration lives inside its own module/submodule (frontend `manifest.ts` + nwidart backend routes + frontend pages).
- Frontend kernel matches WebinoDashboard (`frontend/modules/*/manifest.ts` + `frontend/src/kernel`) so module UIs can be shared across products.
- Public and admin UIs are **SSR**. Target first meaningful paint / LCP under **1 second** on a typical VPS path (cache public GETs, avoid client waterfalls).
- Mobile-first and responsive for all breakpoints (sm/md/lg/xl). Do not ship desktop-only layouts.

## Pages (official shadcn blocks)

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add login-04
npx shadcn@latest add sidebar-07
```

Never hand-draw login or sidebar “inspired by” shadcn. Always add from the official CLI and import the generated components.

Admin shell lives under `/admin`. Keep `/dashboard` → `/admin` redirects for compatibility.

## Forbidden

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hard-coded copy / placeholder
<button>ثبت نام</button>
<div>Coming soon</div>

// ✅ GOOD — translation key + real implementation
<button>{t("auth.register")}</button>
```
